---
import Install from './Install.astro';
import Mark from './Mark.astro';
---

<section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
  <Mark size={48} />
  <h2 id="closing-title">Run your first lane</h2>
  <p>
    Install devlanes, describe your stack in a <code>devlanes.yaml</code> at the root of the
    repository, run <code>devlanes start</code>.
  </p>
  <Install id="install-again" />
  <div class="closing-facts">
    <p>
      devlanes is in beta. Apache-2.0, written in Rust, for macOS, Linux and Windows 11. It runs
      Node, Bun, Deno, Python and Rust services, with presets for Vite, Next, Wrangler and Tauri,
      and Compose files or plain containers as infra.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lanes keep ports, hostnames and data apart; they are not a sandbox, every process runs as you.
      A crashed service stays stopped until you start it again. A remote connection mirrors TCP only
      and never runs commands on the box.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
